@startuml
' Primary presentation of the Components-and-Connectors key view (Figure 3).
' Authored in Slice 2. Renders through scripts/render-diagrams.sh.
' Connectors are first-class: the Inventory Exchange Protocol (IEP) is a named
' provided interface drawn as a lollipop/port on the CFE pub-sub event bus; the
' Outbox, the CFE event store and the databases are queue and store shapes; every
' edge is labelled with its connector type and protocol.
!include style.puml
title Components-and-Connectors view: primary presentation

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
left to right direction
skinparam nodesep 12
skinparam ranksep 34

' ---- store side (one store, drawn in full, x N) -------------------------------
actor "Store\nmanager" as SMGR
node "External\nPOS system" as POS #6FA8DC

rectangle "Store  (one of N: 3 now, up to 10)" as STORE {
  component "POS Adapter" as POSAD #6FA8DC
  component "Store Agent" as SA #93C47D
  database "Store-Local\nInventory" as SLI #8E7CC3
  queue "Outbox" as OB #8E7CC3
}

' ---- distribution center ------------------------------------------------------
rectangle "Distribution Center" as DCB {
  component "Communications\nFront-End\n(pub-sub event bus)" as CFE #F1C232
  interface "IEP\n(publish, ack)" as IEPIF
  interface "IEP\n(subscribe, deliver)" as DLV
  database "CFE event\nstore" as CFEDB #8E7CC3
  component "DC Agent" as DCA #F1C232
  component "Central Master\nInventory" as CMI #F1C232
  database "Master\ninventory DB" as CMIDB #8E7CC3
  component "Shipping-Order\nFulfillment" as SOF #F1C232
  component "Store-Tracking\nClient" as STC #F1C232
  component "Reporting Client" as RC #F1C232
}
actor "DC\nmanager" as DMGR
node "External Analytics\nClient (future\nsubscriber)" as ANLY #6FA8DC

' the CFE provides the IEP on two ports (lollipops): a publish/acknowledge side and
' a subscribe/deliver side
CFE -- IEPIF
CFE -- DLV

' ---- connectors (every edge: <<type>> protocol) -------------------------------
POS --> POSAD : <<event stream>>\nsales records
POSAD --> SA : <<local call>>\nInventory Events
SMGR --> SA : <<request/reply>>\nlocal inventory queries
SA --> SLI : <<data access>>\napply, read
SA --> OB : <<data access>>\nappend (ordered)
OB --> IEPIF : <<pub-sub>> publish\nIEP / TLS 1.3 mutual [secure]
IEPIF --> OB : <<pub-sub>> acknowledge\n[secure]
DCA --> IEPIF : <<pub-sub>> publish\nIEP
CFE --> CFEDB : <<data access>>\npersist, retain
CFEDB --> CFE : <<data access>>\nreplay read
DLV --> CMI : <<pub-sub>> notify
DLV --> SOF : <<pub-sub>> notify
DLV --> STC : <<pub-sub>> notify
DLV --> RC : <<pub-sub>> notify
DLV --> ANLY : <<pub-sub>> notify
CMI --> DLV : <<pub-sub>>\nack (applied through N)
CMI --> CMIDB : <<data access>>
SOF --> CMI : <<request/reply>> read
RC --> CMI : <<request/reply>> query
STC --> CMI : <<request/reply>> query
DMGR --> RC : <<request/reply>> reports
DMGR --> STC : <<request/reply>> store status

' keep the DC manager to the right of the client components, clear of the IEP ports and labels
CMIDB -[hidden]down- DMGR

note bottom of CFE
  The CFE is the pub-sub event bus of the Publish-Subscribe pattern
  (Bass, Clements, and Kazman 129-130). It provides one interface, the
  Inventory Exchange Protocol. Publishers (store Outboxes x N, the DC
  Agent) publish and are acknowledged; every subscriber receives every
  event, filters locally, and acknowledges a cumulative cursor (applied
  through sequence N per source). The event store retains each accepted
  event until every subscription has acknowledged past it plus a
  retention window, and serves the replay read path to a subscriber that
  fell behind or restarted.
end note

legend right
|= Notation |= Meaning |
| green fill | store-side runtime component |
| gold fill | distribution-center runtime component |
| blue fill | external system or boundary element |
| purple database / queue | durable, ordered persistent store |
| circle on a stalk (lollipop) | a provided interface (port) a connector attaches to |
| stick figure | human role (store or DC manager), not a component |
| <<pub-sub>> | the n-ary publish-subscribe connector (the IEP) |
| <<event stream>> | a one-way stream of events, no reply |
| <<request/reply>> | a synchronous request and reply |
| <<data access>> | a component reading or writing its own store |
| <<local call>> | in-process hand-off between a component and its boundary element |
| [secure] | a store-to-DC network leg over TLS 1.3 with mutual certificates |
endlegend
@enduml
